@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] asset-bundle-boundary
Runtime JavaScript and CSS dependencies MUST enter through the esbuild
`js/app.js` and `css/app.css` entry points. Terminal rendering MUST NOT depend
on a runtime CDN, external script tag or inline template script. The CSS entry
MUST import every stylesheet the templates and hooks depend on.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;product] no-external-resources
Every stylesheet, script, font and image the application serves MUST come from
the application origin. Stylesheets and templates MUST NOT reference external
URLs for resources; vendored upstream files keep their notices but are never
loaded from a remote host. The browser probe fails on any cross-origin request.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] four-token-theme
Presentation colour MUST derive only from `--text-color`, `--text-color-alt`,
`--background-color` and `--background-color-alt`, each defined for the light
and dark themes in `css/tokens.css`. State and severity MUST be conveyed by
text, weight or inverse video, never by colour alone. Canvas consumers
(terminal, diagrams, progress bar) MUST read the same tokens.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:product] grid-alignment
Layout MUST use the character grid: horizontal sizes in `ch`, vertical sizes
in multiples of `--line-height`, borders of `--border-thickness`. Renderer-owned
DOM (xterm, SVG diagrams) and overlays are the only elements allowed off the
grid; the probe asserts zero off-grid elements on the workspace routes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] terminal-browser-untrusted-bytes
Guest output MUST reach xterm as bytes, never HTML. The terminal integration
MUST refuse guest clipboard reads (there is no opt-in), bound and consent-gate
clipboard writes, copy selections only to the user's own clipboard, and open
only confirmed HTTP/HTTPS links through supported xterm APIs. Titles remain
browser-local. Rendering an escape sequence is not authorization to invoke a
browser capability. See ADR-0084.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:protocol] terminal-browser-authorized-geometry
Terminal v2 MUST send actual visible-pane geometry through its versioned resize
control only after read/write attachment acknowledgement. Read-only viewers MUST
NOT resize another user's PTY. See ADR-0082 and ADR-0084.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:build] browser-entry-esm
The application JavaScript bundle MUST retain ES-module output and the root
layout MUST load it as a module. Bundled noVNC asynchronous codec detection MUST
remain supported without rewriting upstream source or loading remote scripts.
